# Cloudflare Pages reads this from the Ladle build output, like `_redirects`. It ships from
# `.ladle/static/` rather than `public/` for the reason `robots.txt` beside it records.
#
# A header reaches what a `<meta>` cannot. Ladle generates its own `index.html`, and
# `meta.json`, the hashed assets and the fonts are each a fetchable URL with no document to
# carry a tag. `/*` covers all of them, the SPA fallback included.
#
# `noindex` alone, deliberately — no `nofollow`. Nothing here links anywhere a crawler should
# be stopped from following.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
